    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0127" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.001 Selassie I/377</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Egypt</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 280</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-10-27">October 27,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>There are enclosed two communications addressed by the President to His Imperial
                    Majesty Haile Selassie I, Emperor of Ethiopia.<anchor n="38" xml:id="d132-f1"/>
                    It is <pb facs="0128" n="116" xml:id="pg116"/> desired that these two
                    communications be forwarded by the Legation to the Consul at Asmara, Eritrea, by
                    safe means and that the Legation request the Consul at Asmara to arrange for the
                    transmission of these communications by safe means to the Emperor of Ethiopia at
                    Addis Ababa.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d132-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d132-f1" n="38" xml:id="d132-f1-content">
                <p>Dated July 23, and October 23, <ref target="#pg114">p. 114</ref> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>, respectively.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d132-f2" n="39" xml:id="d132-f2-content">
                <p>The letters were delivered to the Emperor on December 3, 1942, by Colonel Clark
                    of the American Mission at Asmara.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
